{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["Some say that on the first of [Adar] (some say: of Shevat) Moses died, and they say: they mourned thirty days and stayed there six Sabbaths — and this is their proof: \"on this very day,\" for on a single day he read this entire book to all Israel, and on it he died. But this is no proof, for \"on this very day\" refers to the Song. And behold it is written: \"You are crossing the Jordan today.\"" "<b>In the fortieth.</b> I explained it in the portion of Naso."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Bracketed [Adar] is a variant reading; ס״א = 'some say.' The word שתי ('two') is marked with צ״ל ('read:') as שש ('six'). The verse citations are to Deuteronomy 32:48 (הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה) and Deuteronomy 9:1 / 27:2 (אַתָּה עֹבֵר הַיּוֹם); Ibn Ezra leaves them implicit."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:48.981663411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}